t and use that, but that would require `batchInsert()` to call `execute()` itself. That's probably not a change you want to make, right? But if `batchInsert()` is just a convenience function, is there any reason not to include a call to `execute()`? What other possible method could be called after `batchInsert()`? Wrapping both `QueryBuilder()->execute()` would make it easier for each DBMS to use the most efficient methods of mass inserts such as prepared statements.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/comments/44014930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"lrcg","id":2688472,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2ODg0NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2688472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg","html_url":"https://github.com/lrcg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrcg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":126711893,"node_id":"MDEzOkFzc2lnbmVkRXZlbnQxMjY3MTE4OTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/events/126711893","actor":{"login":"samdark","id":47294,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3Mjk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47294?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samdark","html_url":"https:/